{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc | sed -n '155,205p'\nnl -ba test/dao/space/transactor_test.cljc | sed -n '35,115p;195,285p;515,570p'\nrg -n 'stream-values|carrier|dated|correction|2026-09-09' collab/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | head -30\nrg -n 'append-only.*file|file.*reopen|daostream/gap|closed bounded result DaoStream|ds/append\"'!|:transactor.*stream'\"' docs/design/dao.space.md docs/design/dao.space.schema.md docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md\"","aggregated_output":"   155\t            answer)))))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn create!\n   159\t  \"Create a transactor value from a spec — the value, or a throw: the\n   160\t   failure modes are a malformed spec and a malformed retained history,\n   161\t   both of which a caller can only abort on.\n   162\t\n   163\t   Validates surfaces, never retention (D2/T18): stream/reader? and\n   164\t   stream/writer? check the dao.stream reader and writer surfaces, and\n   165\t   neither establishes the complete-retention transport the history scan\n   166\t   requires. The host composition supplies a handle created by\n   167\t   dao.stream.memory-log/create!; supplying an evicting transport is a\n   168\t   host-assembly defect — detectable, deliberately not checked, because a\n   169\t   type check would couple dao.space to memory-log by name and reject a\n   170\t   future correct complete-retention transport.\"\n   171\t  [spec]\n   172\t  (when-not (map? spec)\n   173\t    (throw\n   174\t      (ex-info\n   175\t        \"transactor spec must be a map\"\n   176\t        {:spec spec})))\n   177\t  (let [{:keys [local-stream intake-pool name]} spec]\n   178\t    (when (contains? spec :next-t)\n   179\t      (throw\n   180\t        (ex-info\n   181\t          \"the transactor derives transaction time from retained history; :next-t is not accepted\"\n   182\t          {:spec spec})))\n   183\t    (when-not (and (stream/reader? local-stream)\n   184\t                   (stream/writer? local-stream))\n   185\t      (throw\n   186\t        (ex-info\n   187\t          \"transactor spec requires a :local-stream satisfying the dao.stream reader and writer surfaces\"\n   188\t          {:spec spec})))\n   189\t    (when-not (and (coll? intake-pool) (seq intake-pool))\n   190\t      (throw\n   191\t        (ex-info\n   192\t          \"transactor spec requires a non-empty :intake-pool of streams satisfying the dao.stream writer surface\"\n   193\t          {:spec spec})))\n   194\t    (doseq [intake intake-pool]\n   195\t      (when-not (stream/writer? intake)\n   196\t        (throw\n   197\t          (ex-info\n   198\t            \"transactor :intake-pool members must satisfy IDaoStreamWriter\"\n   199\t            {:intake-pool intake-pool}))))\n   200\t    (let [t (derive-next-t (index/snapshot-datoms local-stream))]\n   201\t      {:dao.space/transactor true\n   202\t       :local-stream local-stream\n   203\t       :intake-pool intake-pool\n   204\t       :name (or name \"transactor\")\n   205\t       :next-t (atom t)\n    35\t(defrecord WriterOnlyStream\n    36\t  []\n    37\t\n    38\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n    39\t\n    40\t  (append! [_this _val] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defrecord RecordingAppendStream\n    44\t  [inner records]\n    45\t\n    46\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n    47\t\n    48\t  (append! [_this val] (swap! records conj val) (stream/append! inner val))\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    52\t\n    53\t  (cursor [_this anchor] (stream/cursor inner anchor))\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t  (next [_this cursor] (stream/next inner cursor)))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(defrecord FailingAppendStream\n    60\t  [inner failures]\n    61\t\n    62\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n    63\t\n    64\t  (append!\n    65\t    [_this packet]\n    66\t    (if (pos? (swap! failures dec))\n    67\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}\n    68\t      (stream/append! inner packet)))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    72\t\n    73\t  (cursor [_this anchor] (stream/cursor inner anchor))\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t  (next [_this cursor] (stream/next inner cursor)))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defrecord ThrowingAppendStream\n    80\t  [inner throw?]\n    81\t\n    82\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n    83\t\n    84\t  (append!\n    85\t    [_this val]\n    86\t    (if @throw?\n    87\t      (do (reset! throw? false)\n    88\t          (throw (ex-info \"simulated transport failure\" {})))\n    89\t      (stream/append! inner val)))\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    93\t\n    94\t  (cursor [_this anchor] (stream/cursor inner anchor))\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t  (next [_this cursor] (stream/next inner cursor)))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defrecord NonOutcomeAppendStream\n   101\t  [inner garbage?]\n   102\t\n   103\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   104\t\n   105\t  (append!\n   106\t    [_this val]\n   107\t    (if @garbage?\n   108\t      (do (reset! garbage? false)\n   109\t          :boom)\n   110\t      (stream/append! inner val)))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   114\t\n   115\t  (cursor [_this anchor] (stream/cursor inner anchor))\n   195\t                          {:result r})))))))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(defn- tx-ts\n   199\t  \"The transaction times of every atomic record currently on a local stream.\"\n   200\t  [local]\n   201\t  (map (comp :t :dao.space/transaction) (stream-values local)))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t(defn- local-still-open?\n   205\t  \"An open memory-log blocks at its tail; a closed one answers end. This is\n   206\t   the observable difference now that v2 lists no closed? predicate.\"\n   207\t  [local]\n   208\t  (= :dao.stream/blocked\n   209\t     (:dao.stream/outcome\n   210\t       (stream/next local\n   211\t                    (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor local :dao.stream/newest))))))\n   212\t\n   213\t\n   214\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   215\t;; Spec validation\n   216\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   217\t\n   218\t(deftest spec-validation\n   219\t  (let [intake (open-intake 4096)]\n   220\t    (testing \"a non-map spec throws the clean malformed-spec diagnostic\"\n   221\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   222\t                               :clj Exception\n   223\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   224\t                            #\"must be a map\"\n   225\t            (transactor/create! 42))))\n   226\t    (testing \"a missing or non-stream :local-stream throws\"\n   227\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   228\t                               :clj Exception\n   229\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   230\t                            #\"local-stream\"\n   231\t            (transactor/create! {:intake-pool [intake]})))\n   232\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   233\t                               :clj Exception\n   234\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   235\t                            #\"local-stream\"\n   236\t            (transactor/create! {:local-stream 42,\n   237\t                                 :intake-pool [intake]})))\n   238\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   239\t                               :clj Exception\n   240\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   241\t                            #\"local-stream\"\n   242\t            (transactor/create! {:local-stream (->ReaderOnlyStream),\n   243\t                                 :intake-pool [intake]})))\n   244\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   245\t                               :clj Exception\n   246\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   247\t                            #\"local-stream\"\n   248\t            (transactor/create! {:local-stream (->WriterOnlyStream),\n   249\t                                 :intake-pool [intake]}))))\n   250\t    (testing \"the intake pool must be a non-empty collection of writers\"\n   251\t      (let [local (open-local)]\n   252\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   253\t                                 :clj Exception\n   254\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   255\t                              #\"intake-pool\"\n   256\t              (transactor/create! {:local-stream local})))\n   257\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   258\t                                 :clj Exception\n   259\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   260\t                              #\"non-empty\"\n   261\t              (transactor/create! {:local-stream local,\n   262\t                                   :intake-pool []})))\n   263\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   264\t                                 :clj Exception\n   265\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   266\t                              #\"intake-pool\"\n   267\t              (transactor/create! {:local-stream local,\n   268\t                                   :intake-pool :nope})))\n   269\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   270\t                                 :clj Exception\n   271\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   272\t                              #\"IDaoStreamWriter\"\n   273\t              (transactor/create! {:local-stream local,\n   274\t                                   :intake-pool [(->ReaderOnlyStream)]})))\n   275\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   276\t                                 :clj Exception\n   277\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   278\t                              #\"IDaoStreamWriter\"\n   279\t              (transactor/create! {:local-stream local,\n   280\t                                   :intake-pool [42]})))))\n   281\t    (testing \":name is optional and diagnostic only\"\n   282\t      (let [local (open-local)]\n   283\t        (is (some? (transactor/create! {:local-stream local,\n   284\t                                        :intake-pool [intake]})))\n   285\t        (is (some? (transactor/create! {:local-stream local,\n   515\t            (transactor/append! log {:db/id 1}))))))\n   516\t\n   517\t\n   518\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   519\t;; Failure handling\n   520\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   521\t\n   522\t(deftest append-failure-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry\n   523\t  (let [local (open-local)\n   524\t        flaky (->FailingAppendStream local (atom 2))\n   525\t        log (open-with-intake flaky)]\n   526\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}\n   527\t           (transactor/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))\n   528\t        \"a refused local append is returned as data, not thrown\")\n   529\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   530\t            :dao.space/t 0,\n   531\t            :dao.space/datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   532\t           (transactor/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))\n   533\t        \"retry lands at the same t: the failed append never advanced it\")\n   534\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   535\t            :dao.space/t 1,\n   536\t            :dao.space/datoms [[2 :test/b 2 1 1]]}\n   537\t           (transactor/append! log {:db/id 2, :test/b 2})))))\n   538\t\n   539\t\n   540\t(deftest append-throw-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry\n   541\t  (let [local (open-local)\n   542\t        throwing (->ThrowingAppendStream local (atom true))\n   543\t        log (open-with-intake throwing)]\n   544\t    (is (thrown? #?(:cljd Object\n   545\t                    :clj Exception\n   546\t                    :cljs js/Error)\n   547\t          (transactor/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})))\n   548\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   549\t            :dao.space/t 0,\n   550\t            :dao.space/datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   551\t           (transactor/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))\n   552\t        \"a thrown underlying error leaves the watermark unchanged\")))\n   553\t\n   554\t\n   555\t(deftest append-folds-a-non-outcome-answer-to-transport-error\n   556\t  (let [local (open-local)\n   557\t        garbage (->NonOutcomeAppendStream local (atom true))\n   558\t        log (open-with-intake garbage)]\n   559\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   560\t            :dao.stream/answer :boom}\n   561\t           (transactor/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))\n   562\t        \"a local append answering a non-outcome is folded to transport-error\n   563\t           with the raw answer retained\")\n   564\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   565\t            :dao.space/t 0,\n   566\t            :dao.space/datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   567\t           (transactor/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))\n   568\t        \"the fold did not advance the watermark: the retry commits at the\n   569\t           original t\")))\n   570\t\n1:Completed-GMT: 2026-09-09 12:31 GMT\n2:Completed-Local: 2026-09-09 19:31 +0700 (Asia/Bangkok)\n40:**r4** took four corrections: validate-before-interpret in `snapshot-datoms`\n241:   unvalidated result is how a loop ends up recurring on a nil cursor.\"\n258:   finish the read at the tail. Each element is validated and flattened as it\n435:| T16 | Intake pool members are validated with v2 `stream/writer?`; a non-empty collection is required | `[D]` |\n452:| S8 | Each element is validated and flattened as it is read, so the first defect in stream order is the one reported and no read happens past it | **`[T→D]`, kept** |\n561:| :118 | `(count (ds/->seq nil (:local agent)))` — entity-id allocation | the v2 `stream-values` count over the local handle | 2 |\n573:`stream-values` loop, generalizing the existing `intake-values` (:126); all 22\n597:- The other **27 migrate**, including `index_test:777`'s descriptor carrier —\n600:  data on an ordinary stream and nothing about a carrier needs complete\n601:  retention. **Corrected (2026-09-09, phase 2 r2): the carrier migrates in\n604:  deftests §5.4 #8 moves; migrating the carrier in Phase 2 would have broken\n748:| 8 | `published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream` (:759; 783, carrier :777) | P2 | **Moved and modernized.** Keep the `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip and the carrier, now a v2 ring buffer, and open the transported coordinate with `query/open-published!`. Assert the **complete exact coordinate map**; `ds/exact-bound?` (:779) is v1 and is replaced by that equality. |\n763:the eighth, and migrates `stream-values` (:122) and the carrier (:777) —\n766:**Corrected (2026-09-09, phase 2 r2):** this section originally assigned\n767:`stream-values` and the carrier to Phase 2; migrating them then would have\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The API and test corrections are genuine. One sentence in the rewritten crash section still conflates an agent stopping inside a live process with the process itself failing; I’m checking that against the memory-log and intake lifetimes before assigning severity."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.space.md | sed -n '422,465p'\nnl -ba collab/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '586,612p;756,778p'\ngit diff --check\nrg -n 'append-only.*file|file.*reopen|daostream/gap|closed bounded result DaoStream|ds/append\"'!|:transactor.*stream'\"' docs/design/dao.space.md docs/design/dao.space.schema.md docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md\nrg -n 'crash|process-lifetime|intake' docs/design/dao.stream.md docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md src/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.space.md | sed -n '422,465p'\nnl -ba collab/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '586,612p;756,778p'\ngit diff --check\nrg -n 'append-only.*file|file.*reopen|daostream/gap|closed bounded result DaoStream|ds/append\"'!|:transactor.*stream'\"' docs/design/dao.space.md docs/design/dao.space.schema.md docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md\nrg -n 'crash|process-lifetime|intake' docs/design/dao.stream.md docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md src/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"   422\t\n   423\t### Fault Tolerance (Crash-Only Semantics)\n   424\t\n   425\tThe write path is crash-only because it is built from atomic appends and\n   426\timmutable publications — not because anything local is durable:\n   427\t\n   428\t- **Atomicity:** every write is one atomic transaction record through one\n   429\t  local append (`dao.space.transactor`), and every publication is an\n   430\t  immutable, content-addressed manifest appended after its node blobs. A\n   431\t  crash can leave a prefix, never a torn transaction or a partial manifest.\n   432\t- **What survives a crash:** un-published local-stream contents do **not**\n   433\t  survive process failure — the local stream is a process-lifetime\n   434\t  `dao.stream` memory-log. Durability begins at publication: what a\n   435\t  DaoJing observer has materialized into `dao.jing` is durable,\n   436\t  append-only, and content-addressed, so published state has no\n   437\t  partial-update corruption window (see *The Write Path* above, and\n   438\t  `dao.space.transactor.md`, *Where durability lives*).\n   439\t- **Reader behavior:** a reader tailing a crashed writer's local stream\n   440\t  simply reaches the tail and is told `:dao.stream/blocked`; it waits for\n   441\t  new data rather than failing. The same holds for a DaoJing observer over\n   442\t  an intake stream.\n   443\t- **Recovery after restart:** a restarted process sees a new, empty local\n   444\t  logical stream with a new identity, so recovery starts from published\n   445\t  state — the agent reads the manifest addresses it (or its configuration)\n   446\t  names and continues from there. Resuming an interrupted publication is\n   447\t  idempotent by construction: content addressing deduplicates a re-emitted\n   448\t  prefix, and the manifest is appended last. The future relief for\n   449\t  un-published history is a causality-carrying checkpoint carried by the\n   450\t  log itself — named as future work in `dao.space.transactor.md`, *Open\n   451\t  items*, and deliberately not designed here.\n   452\t\n   453\t## Coordination: Stigmergy\n   454\t\n   455\tAgents coordinate by leaving datoms in `dao.jing` for others to query, decoupled in time and\n   456\tidentity.\n   457\t\n   458\t**An interpreter taps a stream without being aware of its source.** This is the property that\n   459\tmakes the coordination stigmergic rather than merely asynchronous, and it is the test to apply\n   460\twhen a design looks decoupled but is not. If an interpreter must be *handed* a particular\n   461\tproducer's stream, then something knows both sides and wired them together; the coupling has\n   462\tmoved from a function call to a reference, and has not been removed. The ant is not handed a\n   463\tpheromone trail. It encounters the medium and finds what is there.\n   464\t\n   465\tTwo consequences follow, and both are invariants:\n   586\t| `query_test.cljc` | 2 | 0 (Phase 2) |\n   587\t| `index_test.cljc` | 41 | 0 (Phase 3) |\n   588\t| `stigmergy_test.clj` | 6 | 3 after Phase 2, **0** after Phase 3 |\n   589\t\n   590\t### 4.5 The ring-buffer site accounting\n   591\t\n   592\t- **28** unbounded `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer}` sites.\n   593\t  `query_test:97` is a literal map passed to `q` to prove a raw map is rejected\n   594\t  as a db input — not an open, and unchanged.\n   595\t- `schema_test:304` stays v1: a closed v1 realization for `schema/current`'s\n   596\t  borrowed-input path, which is schema's own surface.\n   597\t- The other **27 migrate**, including `index_test:777`'s descriptor carrier —\n   598\t  the one migrated site that becomes a **v2 ring buffer** rather than a\n   599\t  memory-log, because the point of that test is that a coordinate is ordinary\n   600\t  data on an ordinary stream and nothing about a carrier needs complete\n   601\t  retention. **Corrected (2026-09-09, phase 2 r2): the carrier migrates in\n   602\t  Phase 3, not Phase 2.** Its only caller is\n   603\t  `published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream`, one of the adapter\n   604\t  deftests §5.4 #8 moves; migrating the carrier in Phase 2 would have broken\n   605\t  a v1 test Phase 3 owns.\n   606\t- `index_test:379`'s capacity-bearing gap fixture is **deleted** with S5 (§7).\n   607\t- Every other migrated site is a `dao.space` local stream and becomes\n   608\t  `memory-log/create!`. There is no capacity to choose: the transport declares\n   609\t  no capacity key, and passing `:dao.stream.memory-log/capacity` is\n   610\t  `invalid-spec` by construction.\n   611\t\n   612\t### 4.6 Proof\n   756\tpropagates and the store is closed **exactly once**.\n   757\t\n   758\t### 5.5 Residue\n   759\t\n   760\t`index_test`: after Phase 2 migrates `open-local` (:68) and\n   761\t`MalformedResultStream` (:25) and deletes the gap fixture (:375-392), and\n   762\tPhase 3 removes the seven adapter deftests, strips the fixture and open from\n   763\tthe eighth, and migrates `stream-values` (:122) and the carrier (:777) —\n   764\twhose only callers are the four published-adapter deftests §5.4 #3/#4/#7/#8\n   765\tmove or delete — `grep -c \"ds/\"` returns **0** (41 before Phase 2).\n   766\t**Corrected (2026-09-09, phase 2 r2):** this section originally assigned\n   767\t`stream-values` and the carrier to Phase 2; migrating them then would have\n   768\tpointed a v2 read loop at a v1 `PublishedIndexStream` that has no `cursor`,\n   769\tred-laning Phase 2. Phase 2 lands at 35, and the pair migrates with the\n   770\tadapter deftests above.\n   771\t\n   772\t`stigmergy_test.clj`: Phase 2 clears :103, :106 and :118; Phase 3 clears\n   773\t:176-178. `grep -c \"ds/\"` returns **0** (currently 6). A non-zero count in\n   774\teither means a property was migrated by hand instead of by rule.\n   775\t\n   776\t### 5.6 Proof\n   777\t\n   778\t`schema_test` W38–W41 (:1449, :1481, :1522) must pass **unmodified** — they\ndocs/design/dao.space.transactor.md:39:                              :intake-pool [intake] ; supplied, never owned\ndocs/design/dao.space.transactor.md:76:| T7 | Close is per value: it rejects further writes and neither closes nor erases the local stream or the intake pool |\ndocs/design/dao.space.transactor.md:146:and it is **not durable**: `memory-log` is process-lifetime, and a restarted\ndocs/design/dao.space.transactor.md:153:  intake stream and a DaoJing observer materializes them into content\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'stream-values' test/dao/space/index_test.cljc\nrg -n 'carrier|published-index-is-a-transportable' test/dao/space/index_test.cljc\nsed -n '410,455p' docs/design/dao.stream.md\nsed -n '130,180p' docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md\ndate -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'; TZ=Asia/Bangkok date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %z (Asia/Bangkok)'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'stream-values' test/dao/space/index_test.cljc\nrg -n 'carrier|published-index-is-a-transportable' test/dao/space/index_test.cljc\nsed -n '410,455p' docs/design/dao.stream.md\nsed -n '130,180p' docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md\ndate -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'; TZ=Asia/Bangkok date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %z (Asia/Bangkok)'\"","aggregated_output":"128:(defn- stream-values\n751:             (is (= expected-eavt (stream-values published))))\n757:             (is (= expected-eavt (stream-values published))\n774:           (is (= [] (stream-values published)))\n832:          (is (= eager (stream-values published))\n878:                         (stream-values published)))\n848:(deftest published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream\n866:               carrier (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})]\n870:           (ds/append! carrier transported)\n871:           (is (= descriptor (:ok (ds/next carrier {:position 0}))))\nit was given. It receives the operation as an ordinary argument from the\ncomposition that wired it, exactly as it receives the streams it reads and the\npolicies it applies, and it then depends on a function it was handed rather\nthan on a transport it detected. Such an interpreter is composed for a\nparticular medium and says so; it is not contract-generic code, and nothing\ncontract-generic may be built on it.\n\nThe reader surface is a promise: the handle presents its elements as\none positioned, append-only, retained sequence that cursors can observe and\nre-observe. A transport whose medium retains nothing cannot make that\npromise and has no reader surface: its inbound events are deposited by the\nhost's adapter onto the stream the host composition wired for that boundary\n— where the reading model applies in full. The log lives beside such a\ntransport, composed explicitly by the host, never hidden inside the\ntransport. A deposit destination must admit every valid boundary event per\nits declared retention; wiring one that can refuse is a host assembly\ndefect. Deposit admission is declared, never interrogated: the contract's\npublic surface has no way to ask a handle its retention policy. A constructor\ntakes the deposit destination and its admission declaration as data. This is\nconfiguration provenance, not runtime introspection. (`dao.stream.ws.md`\nspecifies one such transport and the admission rule in detail.)\n\nA boundary that can no longer deposit must make itself **observably gone**. Its\none permitted action is closing the host resource it itself holds; it invokes\nnothing above itself, retries nothing, and interprets nothing. This is the sole\naction a boundary adapter takes beyond appending, and it is not a judgement\nabout any event — it is the same action for every cause. One corner is\nirreducible: when the deposit that failed was the boundary's only channel, the\nrecord of its own departure has nowhere to land, and the failure is observable\nonly to whoever holds the deposit result and through subsequent operations on\nthe handle.\n\nA transport also declares **which outcomes it produces**, and for each one it\nexcludes, why. There are three honest reasons: the outcome's precondition is\nimpossible by the transport's nature (an unbounded log never evicts, so never\nreports `gap`); another policy answers the same condition, named (a ring buffer\nevicts rather than refusing, so pressure surfaces as a `gap` to a cursor that\nspans the eviction, and never as `full`); or the answer is displaced to another channel, named (a transport\nthat cannot know a remote answer at call time reports it as data elsewhere). An\nexclusion with no stated reason is an unimplemented outcome, not a declaration.\n\n### Where the asynchrony goes\n\nThe IO Model makes this contract non-blocking; hosts are asynchronous\nwhether or not it is. A network message arrives when the runtime says so, in\na callback, on a thread or event loop DaoStream does not own. DaoStream does\n  transport a fresh `:oldest` *is* the origin, and the transactor does not\n  create the local stream, so it could not mint at origin even if it wanted\n  to. The mechanism is for consumers on transports that can evict.\n\nSo the residual risk is real and accepted deliberately: a wrongly wired\nevicting transport's surviving suffix would be read and reported as the\nwhole history, silently. A `stream/reader?`/`stream/writer?` surface check\ndoes not establish retention — the defence is this requirement being written\nwhere someone wiring a composition will read it: here, in\n`dao.space.index.md` (*The snapshot* / *The agent-transactor loop*), in\n`dao.space.md` (*The Write Path*), and in ADR 0003's amendment.\n\n## Where durability lives\n\nThe local stream is the **authoritative record for the logical stream's\nlifetime** — the watermark and every published index are derived from it —\nand it is **not durable**: `memory-log` is process-lifetime, and a restarted\nprocess sees a new, empty logical stream with a new identity. That is the\ncorrect shape, not a shortfall:\n\n- **Stage 1, append** — the write lands in the agent's local stream and no\n  storage handle is touched.\n- **Stage 2, publish** — the covered indexes and manifest are appended to an\n  intake stream and a DaoJing observer materializes them into content\n  storage.\n\n**The durable record is what publication puts in `dao.jing`.** Un-published\nwrites are not durable, and never were — v1's local streams were in-memory\nring buffers, so this was equally true before the migration; the design\nmerely claimed otherwise. The pipeline mirrors Datomic's memory-index →\ndisk-index, and a memory index is not durable either. A durable *stream*\ntransport is not the answer and should not be proposed as the fix: it would\nput a second durable record beside the content store, which is exactly the\n`dao.stream`/`dao.jing` unification `dao.space.query.md`'s *Decisions*\nalready ruled out.\n\n## Open items\n\n- **The O(history) watermark replay.** `create!` derives `t` by reading the\n  whole retained history (`index/snapshot-datoms`), and `publish!` rebuilds\n  the indexes from the origin — both correct today *because the transport\n  cannot evict*. The eventual relief keeps one truth — the log carries its\n  own checkpoint, from which the watermark and incremental indexes resume —\n  rather than adding a second stored counter that can disagree with the\n  record. Not designed here.\n- **Schema's migration** (`dao.space.schema.md`, D10) collapses the\n  transitional mixed return — v1 `{:result :ok …}` on success, v2 outcome map\n  on refusal — to the v2 receipt under schema's own plan.\n2026-09-09 12:55:52 GMT\n2026-09-09 19:55:52 +0700 (Asia/Bangkok)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-09 12:55:52 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-09 19:55:52 +0700 (Asia/Bangkok)  \nCoding-Agent: codex  \nSession-ID: 01a080de-1a15-7d23-9a35-4106b127e4f0\n\n# Phase 2 correction review\n\n## P1 — The revised crash section still promises behavior the process-lifetime streams cannot provide\n\n**File:** `docs/design/dao.space.md:439-451`  \n**Blocks the commit:** yes.\n\nThe section now correctly states that unpublished memory-log contents do not survive process failure. Two following claims undermine that correction:\n\n- Lines 439-442 say a reader tailing a “crashed writer’s” local stream reaches `blocked` and waits, and that the same applies to an observer over the intake stream. After process failure, both in-memory handles are gone; nobody can continue tailing them. This is only true when a writer task stops while its host process and stream remain alive.\n- Lines 446-451 place retrying an interrupted publication and a causality-carrying checkpoint under restart recovery. After process failure, unpublished local history may be gone and therefore cannot necessarily be re-emitted. Moreover, the checkpoint in `dao.space.transactor.md` is proposed to reduce O(history) replay; it is not a durability mechanism for unpublished history.\n\n**Concrete change:** distinguish the two failure scopes:\n\n- Within a live process, a stopped writer leaves its still-owned handles readable at their tails, and publication retries are idempotent while the memory-log remains available.\n- On process failure, local and queued-but-unmaterialized data may be lost; recovery has only fully materialized published state.\n- Remove the statement that the future replay checkpoint relieves unpublished-history loss, or explicitly say that it optimizes causality replay and does not add durability.\n\nEverything else in the rewritten section—atomic transaction records, manifest-last publication, and durability beginning only after DaoJing materialization—matches the implementation.\n\n## Corrections confirmed\n\n- `docs/design/dao.space.md:182` now correctly says `q` returns a bounded value and opens or closes nothing.\n- `docs/design/dao.space.md:485-488` now names `transactor/append!`.\n- `docs/design/dao.space.schema.md:246-250` correctly describes a schema wrapper over a transactor value created by `create!`.\n- `docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md:3-7` correctly names the transactor’s explicit operations.\n- The old append-only-file, file-reopen, and `:daostream/gap` claims are gone.\n- The dated plan corrections correctly leave `index_test`’s `stream-values` and descriptor carrier for Phase 3. Their current callers are published-adapter tests that still operate on the v1 adapter.\n- `transactor/create!` checks `map?` before destructuring or calling `contains?`, producing the intended diagnostic for non-map input.\n- The non-map assertion genuinely exercises that guard.\n- `NonOutcomeAppendStream` genuinely exercises the malformed-return branch. Its assertions pin the exact `transport-error` fold, preserve the raw `:boom` answer, and prove via the successful retry at `t=0` that the watermark did not advance.\n- The new double delegates the actual bound `val`; it introduces no repeat of the earlier `ThrowingAppendStream` mistake.\n- `git diff --check` is clean.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Phase 2 is not yet ready to commit.** The code and added tests are cleared, but the remaining process-crash claims in `dao.space.md` must be corrected. The still-running CLJD lane also remains an external readiness gate."}}
